TU1NZ Commercial S8.2 public observer first-start diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-30
Decision: LOCAL_OBSERVER_CONTRACT_FIX_REQUIRED

Observed failure

- The first observer process exited before producing a sample.
- Privacy-safe failure code: HEALTH_TIMER_RED.
- Failed evidence directory:
  /opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s8-public-observation-20260830T173854Z
- The failure happened at the exact health-timer trigger timestamp.

Read-only verification

- tu1nz-adult-public-s7.service remained active/running with NRestarts=0.
- tu1nz-adult-public-s8-telegram.service remained active/running with NRestarts=0.
- tu1nz-adult-public-s8-landing.service remained active/running with NRestarts=0.
- nginx.service remained active/running with NRestarts=0.
- tu1nz-adult-public-s8-health.timer remained active and enabled.
- The triggered health service completed successfully and the timer returned to waiting.
- The external SFW health endpoint remained GREEN with all forbidden capabilities false.

Root cause

The observer required the timer SubState to be exactly waiting. systemd can transiently
move an active timer through a trigger substate while its oneshot target runs. The
observer started on that same trigger second and therefore rejected a healthy timer.

Correction

Bind timer health to the stable contract only:

- ActiveState=active
- systemctl is-enabled returns enabled

The observer remains fail-closed if the timer is inactive or disabled. No service,
proxy, database, token, provider, media, payment or publishing state is changed by
this correction.

Rollback

The previous Control commit remains available and the verified pre-activation backup
continues to cover Control. The failed observer wrote only its dedicated evidence
directory and performed no runtime mutation.
